    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d711">

                <pb facs="0791" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 402.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 399, of
                    the 12th instant, I inclose herewith copies of further memoranda exchanged
                    between the British ambassador and the Department relative to the reference to
                    arbitration of the question of the Japanese Government’s right to impose a house
                    tax in respect to buildings which are held under perpetual lease.</p>
                <p>The Department desires it to be made clear to the Japanese Government that the
                    Government of the United States is of the opinion that the scope of the
                    reference should be such as to include and settle all questions in controversy
                    relative to the imposition of charges and taxes of whatever style and
                    character.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d711-a1.xml" xpointer="d711-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d711-a2.xml" xpointer="d711-a2"/>
